3875 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 512 0 R
/T (around a well-designed relational database. The schema of 11 tables and one view is in Third Normal Form, protected by primary, foreign and unique keys, CHECK constraints, a generated column and purposeful referential actions. The most important business operation, recording a sale, is a single ACID transaction that locks stock rows, validates availability, writes five tables and rolls back completely on any error. Twenty-two SQL queries demonstrate joins, aggregates, GROUP BY / HAVING, subqueries, ROLLUP, a view and a window function, and the web interface turns these queries into dashboards, reports, invoices and a POS screen. The automated suite of 111 API checks passed in full, which gives confidence that the database rules and the application behave as designed.)
/E (around a well-designed relational database. The schema of 11 tables and one view is in Third Normal Form, protected by primary, foreign and unique keys, CHECK constraints, a generated column and purposeful referential actions. The most important business operation, recording a sale, is a single ACID transaction that locks stock rows, validates availability, writes five tables and rolls back completely on any error. Twenty-two SQL queries demonstrate joins, aggregates, GROUP BY / HAVING, subqueries, ROLLUP, a view and a window function, and the web interface turns these queries into dashboards, reports, invoices and a POS screen. The automated suite of 111 API checks passed in full, which gives confidence that the database rules and the application behave as designed.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [37]
>>
endobj
3876 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 512 0 R
/T (Working on the project reinforced that integrity belongs in the database: the CHECK, UNIQUE and FOREIGN KEY constraints caught invalid data even when the application layer was bypassed, and keeping the SQL visible \(no ORM\) made each design decision easy to reason about and to explain.)
/E (Working on the project reinforced that integrity belongs in the database: the CHECK, UNIQUE and FOREIGN KEY constraints caught invalid data even when the application layer was bypassed, and keeping the SQL visible \(no ORM\) made each design decision easy to reason about and to explain.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [38]
>>
endobj
