7443 0 obj
<<
/Title (Small and medium retail stores still run on paper registers or loosely connected spreadsheets. Stock counts drift away from reality, invoices are copied by hand, and the owner cannot answer simple questions such as which products are about to run out or who our best customers are. This project, RetailDesk, designs and implements a complete Retail Inventory and Sales Management System on top of a carefully normalised relational database. The database, retail_inventory_db, runs on MySQL 8.0 \(InnoDB\) and contains 11 tables and 1 view in Third Normal Form. It enforces integrity with 11 foreign keys \(with RESTRICT, CASCADE and SET NULL actions chosen per relationship\), UNIQUE and CHECK constraints, a generated column, and indexes on all search paths. A web application \(React 18 front end, Node.js and Express back end\) lets staff manage products, categories, suppliers, customers and stock; sell through a point-of-sale screen; print GST invoices; track payments; and view dashboards and nine business reports. Every figure on screen is produced by a parameterised SQL query. A sale is written to five tables inside a single ACID transaction with row-level locking, so stock can never be oversold or left half-updated.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7440 0 R
/Next 7447 0 R
>>
endobj
